WEBVTT

00:00:00.301 --> 00:00:03.086
Last video ended on this curve, y equals

00:00:03.206 --> 00:00:05.271
three to the two x, and two other

00:00:05.291 --> 00:00:06.353
composites we haven't done yet.

00:00:07.055 --> 00:00:09.101
Here are two quick answers for its derivative.

00:00:09.785 --> 00:00:11.792
One says two times three to the two

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:11.973
x.

00:00:12.596 --> 00:00:14.285
The other says three to the two x,

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:15.854
times the natural log of three.

00:00:16.719 --> 00:00:18.986
At x equals zero, the first predicts a

00:00:19.027 --> 00:00:19.808
slope of two,

00:00:20.412 --> 00:00:22.578
and the second about one point one zero.

00:00:23.283 --> 00:00:24.530
Let's measure the real slope.

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:28.162
Secants from closer and closer points give four,

00:00:28.504 --> 00:00:30.751
then about two point four six, then about

00:00:30.852 --> 00:00:31.794
two point two two.

00:00:32.477 --> 00:00:34.283
They settle at about two point two.

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:36.019
Neither answer is right.

00:00:36.707 --> 00:00:39.072
So what is the slope, and why does

00:00:39.113 --> 00:00:40.936
a composite like this need more than one

00:00:41.018 --> 00:00:41.378
factor?

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:42.974
Here's where it comes from.

00:00:43.681 --> 00:00:46.086
Three to the two x is three squared,

00:00:46.327 --> 00:00:48.191
to the x, so it's nine to the

00:00:48.351 --> 00:00:48.472
x.

00:00:49.153 --> 00:00:51.177
And you know a to the x has

00:00:51.198 --> 00:00:53.642
derivative a to the x, times the natural

00:00:53.703 --> 00:00:54.223
log of a.

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:56.675
So the slope is nine to the x,

00:00:57.017 --> 00:00:58.363
times the natural log of nine.

00:00:59.109 --> 00:01:01.195
The natural log of nine is two times

00:01:01.236 --> 00:01:02.179
the natural log of three.

00:01:02.802 --> 00:01:05.110
So the derivative is two, times the natural

00:01:05.151 --> 00:01:07.418
log of three, times three to the two

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:07.579
x.

00:01:08.404 --> 00:01:11.036
At zero, that's about two point two, the

00:01:11.057 --> 00:01:11.719
slope we measured.

00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:14.898
Each quick answer kept one factor and lost

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:15.261
the other.

00:01:15.845 --> 00:01:17.103
The picture shows why there are two.

00:01:17.848 --> 00:01:19.955
Three to the two x is three to

00:01:19.995 --> 00:01:22.565
the x, squashed sideways by a half.

00:01:23.247 --> 00:01:25.295
The base three gives the slope its natural

00:01:25.336 --> 00:01:25.957
log of three.

00:01:26.642 --> 00:01:29.117
The squash, from the inside two x, doubles

00:01:29.158 --> 00:01:29.218
it.

00:01:29.761 --> 00:01:32.488
So every composite needs two separate things:

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.577
the outside's slope, worked out at the inside,

00:01:35.998 --> 00:01:37.482
and the inside's own slope.

00:01:38.245 --> 00:01:40.379
Here are the three outsides we haven't used

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:40.580
yet.

00:01:41.385 --> 00:01:42.967
A to the power of an inside:

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:45.652
copy it, times the natural log of a,

00:01:46.093 --> 00:01:47.616
times the inside's derivative.

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:50.080
Log base a of an inside:

00:01:50.622 --> 00:01:53.466
the inside's derivative, over the inside times the

00:01:53.487 --> 00:01:54.367
natural log of a,

00:01:54.889 --> 00:01:56.270
and the inside must be positive.

00:01:57.073 --> 00:01:58.034
Tan of an inside:

00:01:58.777 --> 00:02:01.542
sec squared of the same inside, times the

00:02:01.643 --> 00:02:02.624
inside's derivative,

00:02:03.287 --> 00:02:05.711
and it breaks wherever the inside reaches pi

00:02:05.752 --> 00:02:07.014
over two, plus k pi.

00:02:07.856 --> 00:02:10.641
The outside brings its own fixed part, the

00:02:10.682 --> 00:02:13.006
natural log of a, or sec squared.

00:02:13.768 --> 00:02:16.113
The inside's derivative is an extra factor,

00:02:16.615 --> 00:02:18.598
and the inside also decides the domain.

00:02:19.295 --> 00:02:21.141
Worked example one, from the course.

00:02:21.825 --> 00:02:25.291
Differentiate y equals log base three of, x

00:02:25.332 --> 00:02:27.715
squared plus one, and find the gradient at

00:02:27.997 --> 00:02:28.697
x equals one.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.064
Domain first.

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:33.015
The inside, x squared plus one, is always

00:02:33.116 --> 00:02:35.121
at least one, so it's always positive.

00:02:35.605 --> 00:02:37.601
The function exists for every real x.

00:02:38.348 --> 00:02:40.181
The inside's derivative is two x.

00:02:40.624 --> 00:02:42.607
So d y by d x is two

00:02:42.749 --> 00:02:45.413
x, over x squared plus one, times the

00:02:45.454 --> 00:02:46.475
natural log of three.

00:02:47.318 --> 00:02:50.005
At x equals one, that's two, over two

00:02:50.066 --> 00:02:52.010
times the natural log of three, which is

00:02:52.312 --> 00:02:54.197
one over the natural log of three, about

00:02:54.298 --> 00:02:55.019
point nine one.

00:02:55.722 --> 00:02:57.686
And at x equals zero the top is

00:02:57.707 --> 00:02:59.690
zero, so the curve is flat at its

00:02:59.792 --> 00:03:00.372
lowest point.

00:03:01.116 --> 00:03:02.142
Worked example two.

00:03:02.786 --> 00:03:05.630
Differentiate y equals tan of e to the

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:08.275
x, and say where the derivative exists.

00:03:09.038 --> 00:03:11.262
The inside is e to the x, and

00:03:11.383 --> 00:03:13.187
its derivative is e to the x as

00:03:13.248 --> 00:03:13.407
well.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.117
So d y by d x is e

00:03:16.139 --> 00:03:18.286
to the x, times sec squared of e

00:03:18.508 --> 00:03:18.989
to the x.

00:03:19.778 --> 00:03:20.424
Now the walls.

00:03:21.132 --> 00:03:23.918
Tan breaks where its inside equals pi over

00:03:23.999 --> 00:03:25.342
two, plus k pi.

00:03:25.904 --> 00:03:27.969
But e to the x is always positive,

00:03:28.332 --> 00:03:30.076
so it can only reach the positive ones:

00:03:30.458 --> 00:03:32.383
pi over two, three pi over two, and

00:03:32.424 --> 00:03:32.704
so on.

00:03:33.407 --> 00:03:35.373
So x can't be the natural log of

00:03:35.475 --> 00:03:37.561
pi over two, or the natural log of

00:03:37.582 --> 00:03:39.087
three pi over two, and so on.

00:03:39.771 --> 00:03:41.398
To the left, there are no walls at

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.549
all, and the curve flattens towards zero.

00:03:44.213 --> 00:03:46.621
At x equals zero, the gradient is sec

00:03:46.662 --> 00:03:49.432
squared of one, about three point four three.

00:03:49.948 --> 00:03:51.638
Here's how to keep the constants in the

00:03:51.699 --> 00:03:52.342
right places.

00:03:53.288 --> 00:03:55.911
Powers multiply by the natural log of a,

00:03:56.754 --> 00:03:58.055
logs divide by it,

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:01.560
and the inside's slope always goes on top.

00:04:02.664 --> 00:04:05.352
Powers multiply, because a to the x is

00:04:05.554 --> 00:04:07.660
e to the power of, x times the

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:08.603
natural log of a.

00:04:09.688 --> 00:04:12.496
Logs divide, because log base a of x

00:04:12.939 --> 00:04:15.044
is the natural log of x, over the

00:04:15.085 --> 00:04:15.807
natural log of a.

00:04:16.971 --> 00:04:19.737
And the inside's slope comes from the chain

00:04:19.778 --> 00:04:20.900
rule, every time.

00:04:21.866 --> 00:04:24.480
Try log base seven of, two x plus

00:04:24.521 --> 00:04:24.761
three.

00:04:25.405 --> 00:04:26.427
The two goes on top,

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.217
and two x plus three, times the natural

00:04:29.239 --> 00:04:30.944
log of seven, goes underneath.

00:04:31.589 --> 00:04:33.923
Then check the domain the inside allows.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:37.053
Your turn.

00:04:37.738 --> 00:04:40.499
Find the exact gradient of the curve y

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:42.941
equals five to the x squared, at the

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.883
point where x equals one.

00:04:45.547 --> 00:04:46.380
Pause here to answer.

00:04:57.048 --> 00:04:59.071
The outside is five to the power of

00:04:59.112 --> 00:05:01.817
an inside, so copy it and multiply by

00:05:01.858 --> 00:05:03.200
the natural log of five.

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:06.797
The inside is x squared, so multiply by

00:05:06.919 --> 00:05:07.943
two x as well.

00:05:08.706 --> 00:05:11.248
At x equals one, that's two, times the

00:05:11.289 --> 00:05:13.870
natural log of five, times five, which is

00:05:13.951 --> 00:05:15.852
ten times the natural log of five.

00:05:16.554 --> 00:05:18.719
Five times the natural log of five has

00:05:18.821 --> 00:05:20.425
dropped the inside's two x.

00:05:22.132 --> 00:05:22.477
Last one.

00:05:23.088 --> 00:05:26.816
Differentiate y equals log base two of, four

00:05:26.858 --> 00:05:28.861
minus x, and state its domain.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.282
Pause here to answer.

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:41.634
Domain first:

00:05:42.215 --> 00:05:45.317
the inside must be positive, so four minus

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:47.599
x is positive, and x is less than

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:47.859
four.

00:05:48.662 --> 00:05:50.709
The inside's derivative is minus one.

00:05:51.372 --> 00:05:53.613
So d y by d x is minus

00:05:53.714 --> 00:05:56.755
one, over four minus x, times the natural

00:05:56.816 --> 00:05:58.917
log of two, for x less than four.

00:05:59.819 --> 00:06:01.923
Without the minus, the slope would be positive,

00:06:02.345 --> 00:06:05.050
but this log falls, because its inside shrinks

00:06:05.351 --> 00:06:06.052
as x grows.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:10.445
So for every composite, keep two factors, the

00:06:10.526 --> 00:06:13.391
outside's slope at the inside and the inside's

00:06:13.671 --> 00:06:16.356
own slope, and let the inside decide the

00:06:16.377 --> 00:06:16.637
domain.

00:06:17.518 --> 00:06:19.440
If a question mixes these with a product

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.283
or a quotient, find the last operation first,

00:06:22.443 --> 00:06:24.565
as before, and use these rules for the

00:06:24.605 --> 00:06:25.566
pieces inside it.

00:06:26.188 --> 00:06:28.375
That finishes the derivatives you need for every

00:06:28.415 --> 00:06:29.759
function family in this strand.

00:06:30.462 --> 00:06:33.219
Next, we'll use these derivatives to build lines.

00:06:34.064 --> 00:06:37.012
Here's y equals cos two x, and the

00:06:37.052 --> 00:06:38.957
point where x equals pi over six.

00:06:39.639 --> 00:06:41.941
Its derivative is minus two sine two x,

00:06:42.281 --> 00:06:44.483
so the gradient there is minus root three.

00:06:45.365 --> 00:06:47.933
What line just touches the curve there, and

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:49.739
what line meets it at right angles?

00:06:52.421 --> 00:06:53.264
Here are the key notes.

00:06:53.886 --> 00:06:55.435
Pause the video if you need more time

00:06:55.475 --> 00:06:55.917
to copy them.
